{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "לבני יוסף לבני אפרים", :translit "livnei yosef livnei efrayim", :gloss "of the sons of Joseph, of the sons of Ephraim"} {:he "ולא אמר לבני יוסף לאפרים", :translit "velo amar livnei yosef le'efrayim", :gloss "and it does not say 'of the sons of Joseph, of Ephraim'"} {:he "לבני אפרים", :translit "livnei efrayim", :gloss "of the sons of Ephraim"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Contrastive reading: verse says לבני אפרים instead of simply לאפרים, to match the pattern used for all other tribes."}], :frame {:text "Jacob blessed Ephraim over Manasseh and said his seed shall become a multitude of nations (Genesis 48:19). Ephraim's descendant Joshua led Israel after Moses (Exodus 17:9–10), and the leader of the tribe of Ephraim in the wilderness census was Elishama son of Ammihud (Numbers 1:10). Since Joseph himself was not counted as an independent tribe among the twelve, the tribal standard was identified by his sons' names rather than Joseph's own.", :sources ["Genesis 48:19" "Exodus 17:9–10" "Numbers 1:10"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Contrastive reading: verse says לבני אפרים instead of simply לאפרים, to match the pattern used for all other tribes.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:26:41.125936069Z", :model "glm-5.2"}